.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt PCID 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm pcid
.Nd PCI configuration-space enumerator and the pci: scheme
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm /sbin/pcid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the ACPI boot blob, locates the MCFG table and maps the first 1 MiB of the
ECAM window.  It scans bus 0, records the vendor, device, class, revision and six
32-bit BAR values of every function, prints
.Dq pcid: devices= Ns Ar count
and registers the
.Dq pci:
scheme.
.Pp
Enumeration is limited to bus 0 in this milestone.  The server receives the
RootDevice capability through the
.Ql root
service grant; it is the only process allowed to create
.Dv MmioRegion
objects.
.Pp
The scheme layout is:
.Bl -tag -width Pa -compact
.It Pa /
one packed K60 directory entry per function, named
.Sy bb:ss.f
.Pq bus, slot, function in lowercase hex .
.It Pa /bb:ss.f/info
the 40-byte little-endian device record: bus, slot, function, class, subclass,
programming interface, revision, vendor, device, six BAR words, the interrupt
line and the interrupt pin.
.It Pa /bb:ss.f/bar Ns Ar n
opens a fresh
.Dv MmioRegion
for that 32-bit or 64-bit memory BAR and returns it as an S25 attachment.  I/O
BARs and absent BARs return
.Er ENOENT .
.El
.Pp
Only read access is accepted; every open is a new attachment and the client owns
the returned handle.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d/pcid.toml -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/pcid.toml
service manifest with the
.Ql root
grant
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr devd 8 ,
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr svcd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
server first appeared in RavenBSD 0.1.
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
